DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       _N_o_t_e: these functions are removed in glibc 2.25.

       The  mmaalllloocc__ggeett__ssttaattee()  function records the current state of all mmaall‐‐
       lloocc(3) internal bookkeeping variables (but not the actual  contents  of
       the heap or the state of mmaalllloocc__hhooookk(3) functions pointers).  The state
       is recorded in a system‐dependent opaque data structure dynamically al‐
       located via mmaalllloocc(3), and a pointer to that data structure is returned
       as  the function result.  (It is the caller’s responsibility to ffrreeee(3)
       this memory.)

       The mmaalllloocc__sseett__ssttaattee() function restores the state of all mmaalllloocc(3) in‐
       ternal bookkeeping variables to the values recorded in the opaque  data
       structure pointed to by _s_t_a_t_e.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On  success,  mmaalllloocc__ggeett__ssttaattee() returns a pointer to a newly allocated
       opaque data structure.  On error (for example, memory could not be  al‐
       located for the data structure), mmaalllloocc__ggeett__ssttaattee() returns NULL.

       On  success,  mmaalllloocc__sseett__ssttaattee()  returns 0.  If the implementation de‐
       tects that _s_t_a_t_e does not point to a correctly formed  data  structure,
       mmaalllloocc__sseett__ssttaattee()  returns -1.  If the implementation detects that the
       version of the data structure referred to by _s_t_a_t_e  is  a  more  recent
       version  than  this  implementation knows about, mmaalllloocc__sseett__ssttaattee() re‐
       turns -2.

